; The "unique, or nothing" half of MAC-HYG-8's fourth hole
; (2026-08-16). A template's free identifier naming something the
; macro's module imported resolves to the module that DECLARES it -
; and when more than one module declares it, the rewrite has no more
; right to choose than a bare reference does, so it chooses nothing
; and the name stays bare.
;
; What that produces is `AX3014`: the same ambiguity a bare reference
; draws, reported at the INVOCATION - which mentions neither `dup`
; nor either module - and carrying the expansion frame that names
; `useDup`. The frame is the whole of what makes the line actionable,
; and `AmbMac` imports only `AmbB`: it is THIS file's second import
; that makes the name ambiguous, so the author who must act is here.
;
; This used to have a sibling. `596-macro-capture-in-module` (deleted,
; with its three goldens) held the other way the same rewrite refused
; - `AX3032`, when a binder at the invocation would have captured the
; name left bare - and it is gone as of 2026-08-16: a template's free
; identifier resolves at the macro's own scope now, so nothing at a
; call site can capture it, and the code is retired. Ambiguity is what
; is left, and it is a CHECKER refusal rather than an expansion one,
; which is why this file can carry it alone.
(import AmbMac)

(import AmbA)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (useDup 4))
